    "author": {
        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18408832?u=4369d0200edfcaf24cee3e42033d39ba5d1b5226&v=4",
        "login": "alezunino",
        "resourcePath": "/alezunino",
        "url": "https://github.com/alezunino"
    },
    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hi,\r\nI have noticed that when using mini.base16 colors, some words lack bold style compared to other colorschemes such as catppuccin, using TreeSitter supported languages such as Markdown. This can be fixed by adding this line to base16.lua:\r\n`  \r\nhi('Strong',     {fg=nil,      bg=nil, attr='bold',      sp=nil})\r\n`\r\n\r\nI am not sure whether this is a bug or it is the expected formatting, but I prefer the way catppuccin displays in bold some words.\r\n\r\nthanks",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hi,<br>\nI have noticed that when using mini.base16 colors, some words lack bold style compared to other colorschemes such as catppuccin, using TreeSitter supported languages such as Markdown. This can be fixed by adding this line to base16.lua:<br>\n<code class=\"notranslate\">  hi('Strong',     {fg=nil,      bg=nil, attr='bold',      sp=nil})</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I am not sure whether this is a bug or it is the expected formatting, but I prefer the way catppuccin displays in bold some words.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">thanks</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hi,\nI have noticed that when using mini.base16 colors, some words lack bold style compared to other colorschemes such as catppuccin, using TreeSitter supported languages such as Markdown. This can be fixed by adding this line to base16.lua:\n  hi('Strong',     {fg=nil,      bg=nil, attr='bold',      sp=nil})\nI am not sure whether this is a bug or it is the expected formatting, but I prefer the way catppuccin displays in bold some words.\nthanks",
